USE nepal_disaster_archive;

INSERT IGNORE INTO stories
(title, slug, category_id, event_date, year_label, location, summary, content, deaths, injuries, magnitude, impact, sources, featured, status)
VALUES
('1255 Kathmandu Valley Earthquake','1255-kathmandu-valley-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1255-06-07','1255','Kathmandu Valley','The earliest major earthquake in Nepal for which a historical record survives.','On 7 June 1255 a major earthquake struck the Kathmandu Valley. Historical accounts describe severe destruction of buildings and temples and a very large loss of life. NSET identifies it as the first recorded earthquake in Nepal and reports that King Abhaya Malla died. The commonly cited magnitude of about 7.7 is a reconstruction, not an instrumental measurement.','Historical account: about one third of Kathmandu population; exact number uncertain','Not reliably known','Estimated about 7.7','Buildings and temples collapsed or were severely damaged; wider humanitarian hardship followed.','NSET chronological historical earthquake catalogue',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1260 Nepal Earthquake','1260-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1260-01-01','1260','Kathmandu Valley and surrounding areas','A major earthquake recorded during the Malla period caused heavy loss of life and property.','The 1260 earthquake is one of the earliest major earthquakes in Nepal’s surviving historical record. Contemporary information is limited. NSET records heavy loss of life and property and notes epidemic and famine in the aftermath. Exact date, magnitude and casualty figures are not reliably established.','Heavy loss of life reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Not reliably established','Buildings and temples were damaged or destroyed and wider social hardship was reported.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1408 Nepal Earthquake','1408-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1408-09-01','1408','Kathmandu Valley and surrounding areas','A major historical earthquake caused heavy damage to temples, buildings and settlements.','Historical records place a major earthquake in August or September 1408. NSET records destruction of the Rato Machhindranath temple, damage to many buildings and temples, ground cracks and heavy loss of life and livestock. The exact day and scientific magnitude remain uncertain.','Heavy loss of life reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Estimated about 7.0 in NSET historical catalogue','Temples, buildings, land and livestock were affected.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1681 Nepal Earthquake','1681-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1681-12-01','1681','Kathmandu Valley and Nepal','A major historical earthquake caused loss of life and damage to buildings and temples.','Historical records identify a significant earthquake around December 1681 or January 1682. Available documentation is limited, but NSET records loss of life and property and damage or destruction of buildings and temples.','Heavy loss of life reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Not reliably established','Historic buildings and temples were damaged or destroyed.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1767 Nepal Earthquake Sequence','1767-nepal-earthquake-sequence',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1767-06-01','1767','Nepal including Kathmandu Valley','A significant 1767 earthquake sequence included numerous shocks and aftershocks.','NSET records about 21 shocks and aftershocks within roughly 24 hours in June-July 1767. Surviving records do not support a reliable modern magnitude or casualty total.','Not reliably known','Not reliably known','Not established','Repeated shaking affected buildings and communities.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1810 Nepal Earthquake','1810-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1810-05-01','1810','Nepal and Kathmandu Valley','The 1810 earthquake caused moderate to heavy human and property losses.','A major earthquake was recorded in May 1810. NSET describes moderate to heavy loss of life and property. No reliable instrumental magnitude or precise casualty count exists.','Moderate to heavy loss reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Not reliably established','Buildings and property were damaged.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1823 Nepal Earthquake','1823-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1823-01-01','1823','Nepal','A historical earthquake recorded in 1823 caused loss of life and property, although details are limited.','NSET records a 1823 earthquake with minor loss of life and property. Exact date, magnitude and geographic extent are uncertain.','Minor loss reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Not established','Localized building and property damage was reported.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1833 Nepal Earthquake','1833-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1833-08-26','1833','Kathmandu Valley and central Nepal','The 1833 earthquake sequence was one of the most important pre-instrumental earthquakes in the Kathmandu Valley.','On 26 August 1833 a major earthquake sequence affected Kathmandu and surrounding regions. Historical accounts describe repeated strong shocks and substantial damage. NSET records 18,000 buildings and temples damaged in the broader sequence record. Another strong earthquake occurred on 25 September, with additional shocks in 1834. Modern magnitude estimates are reconstructed and vary.','Casualty estimates vary; no single authoritative total','Not reliably established','Historical estimates vary','About 18,000 buildings and temples were reported damaged in the NSET record.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue; historical and paleoseismic research',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1834 Nepal Earthquake Sequence','1834-nepal-earthquake-sequence',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1834-07-11','1834','Kathmandu Valley and Nepal','Several strong shocks were recorded in 1834 following the destructive 1833 sequence.','Historical records list strong shocks on 11 July, 13 July and 26 September 1834, along with other tremors. NSET describes heavy loss of life and property.','Heavy loss reported; exact number unknown','Unknown','Not reliably established','Repeated earthquakes caused additional structural damage and prolonged disruption.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1934 Nepal-Bihar Earthquake','1934-nepal-bihar-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1934-01-15','1934','Kathmandu Valley, eastern Nepal and Bihar','The 1934 Nepal-Bihar earthquake was one of the most destructive earthquakes in modern South Asian history.','On 15 January 1934 a very large earthquake struck Nepal and northern Bihar. Kathmandu, Bhaktapur and Patan suffered severe structural damage. NSET’s historical table gives a magnitude of about 8.4, 8,519 deaths, 80,893 collapsed buildings and 126,355 damaged buildings. Other sources use different casualty boundaries, so totals should be identified by source.','NSET historical table: 8,519','Widespread; exact total uncertain','About 8.4 historical estimate','Homes, temples, palaces and public buildings collapsed or were damaged across Nepal and Bihar.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue; historical government records',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1980 Bajhang Earthquake','1980-bajhang-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1980-08-04','1980','Bajhang, western Nepal','The 1980 Bajhang earthquake killed and injured hundreds and damaged thousands of buildings.','NSET records a magnitude of about 6.1, 46 deaths and 236 injuries. It also records 12,817 buildings/temples collapsed and 13,298 damaged.','46','236','About 6.1','Thousands of rural buildings were collapsed or damaged.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1988 Udayapur Earthquake','1988-udayapur-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1988-08-21','1988','Udayapur and eastern Nepal','The 1988 Udayapur earthquake caused widespread damage and hundreds of deaths in eastern Nepal.','On 21 August 1988 a major earthquake struck eastern Nepal. Historical Nepal earthquake records commonly report about 721 deaths and magnitude estimates around 6.5. Homes and public buildings were damaged and landslides occurred in affected areas.','About 721 reported','Hundreds reported','About 6.5','Homes, schools and other structures were damaged across eastern Nepal.','NSET earthquake catalogue; Government of Nepal; USGS',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2011 Sikkim Earthquake and Nepal Impacts','2011-sikkim-earthquake-nepal',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2011-09-18','2011','Eastern Nepal and Sikkim region','The 2011 Sikkim earthquake was strongly felt across eastern Nepal.','On 18 September 2011 a magnitude 6.9 earthquake struck the Sikkim region. Strong shaking was experienced in eastern Nepal and landslides and localized structural damage occurred. It is best described as a regional earthquake with impacts in Nepal.','Nepal-only total varies by source','Reported injuries','Mw 6.9','Localized structural damage and landslides affected eastern Nepal.','USGS; Government of Nepal disaster reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2015 Gorkha Earthquake','2015-gorkha-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2015-04-25','2015','Gorkha, Kathmandu Valley and central Nepal','The Mw 7.8 Gorkha earthquake became the defining natural disaster of modern Nepal.','At 11:56 local time on 25 April 2015 a magnitude 7.8 earthquake began about 82 km northwest of Kathmandu. The earthquake generated strong shaking, landslides and avalanches. USGS reports about 9,000 fatalities, about 23,000 injuries, more than 500,000 destroyed houses and about 270,000 damaged houses. A magnitude 7.3 aftershock struck on 12 May. Heritage sites, schools, hospitals, roads and rural mountain communities were severely affected.','About 9,000','About 23,000','Mw 7.8; 12 May aftershock Mw 7.3','More than 500,000 houses destroyed and about 270,000 damaged according to USGS.','USGS; Government of Nepal Post Disaster Needs Assessment; UNESCO; NSET',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2023 Jajarkot Earthquake','2023-jajarkot-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2023-11-03','2023','Jajarkot and Rukum West, Karnali Province','The 2023 Jajarkot earthquake caused major casualties and housing destruction in western Nepal.','On 3 November 2023 a magnitude 5.7 earthquake struck western Nepal. Jajarkot and Rukum West suffered severe damage, especially where vulnerable homes could not withstand shaking. Official post-event assessments recorded 154 deaths and hundreds of injuries, with tens of thousands of houses damaged.','154','Hundreds','Magnitude 5.7','Homes collapsed or were damaged and essential services were disrupted.','USGS; Government of Nepal/NDRRMA post-earthquake assessments',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1978 Tinau Basin Flood','1978-tinau-basin-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'1978-07-01','1978','Tinau Basin and southern Nepal','A major Tinau Basin flood is listed among Nepal’s historical flood disasters.','The 1978 Tinau Basin flood followed intense monsoon rainfall and caused damage along the river system. Nepal government disaster-risk records identify it as a major historical flood. Older reporting is incomplete, so unsupported precise casualty totals are not given here.','Historical totals vary','Not consistently documented','Severe monsoon flood','Settlements, farmland and infrastructure were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1980 Koshi Flood','1980-koshi-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'1980-07-01','1980','Koshi Basin, eastern Nepal','A major Koshi flood in 1980 is recorded among Nepal’s important historical floods.','The Koshi is highly exposed to monsoon flooding because of its huge catchment, steep terrain, sediment loads and dense downstream settlement. The 1980 flood is listed in Nepal government historical disaster records, although exact casualty and economic-loss figures are not consistently reported in surviving summaries.','Historical totals vary','Not consistently documented','Severe monsoon flood','Settlements, farmland and infrastructure in the Koshi basin were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1985 Tadi River Basin Flood','1985-tadi-river-basin-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'1985-07-01','1985','Tadi River Basin','The 1985 Tadi basin flood is recorded among Nepal’s major historical flood disasters.','Heavy monsoon rainfall produced destructive flooding in the Tadi River basin in 1985. Exact casualty and economic-loss figures are not consistently available in national historical summaries.','Historical totals vary','Not consistently documented','Severe monsoon flood','Settlements, agricultural land and river infrastructure were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1987 Sunkoshi Basin Flood','1987-sunkoshi-basin-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'1987-07-01','1987','Sunkoshi Basin','The 1987 Sunkoshi basin flood is included in Nepal’s historical flood record.','The Sunkoshi is vulnerable to flash floods, landslides and debris flows. A major flood in 1987 is listed among the historical flood disasters recorded by Nepal authorities. Precise casualty figures are not consistently available in the national historical summaries.','Historical totals vary','Not consistently documented','Severe monsoon flood','River corridors, settlements, agriculture and transport infrastructure were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1993 Central Nepal Flood and Landslide Disaster','1993-central-nepal-flood-landslide-disaster',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'1993-07-19','1993','Central and southern Nepal','Exceptional monsoon rainfall produced catastrophic floods and landslides across central and southern Nepal.','In July 1993 exceptionally heavy monsoon rainfall triggered widespread floods, flash floods and landslides. Government disaster-risk summaries report more than 1,000 deaths in the event period. Because floods and landslides occurred simultaneously across many districts, totals differ by reporting boundary.','More than 1,000 in national summaries','Thousands reported/affected','Exceptional monsoon rainfall','Roads, bridges, homes, agricultural land and communication links were severely damaged.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal; UN disaster summaries',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2008 Koshi Flood and Embankment Breach','2008-koshi-flood-embankment-breach',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2008-08-18','2008','Kusaha, Sunsari and Koshi Basin','The August 2008 Koshi embankment breach caused catastrophic flooding and large-scale displacement.','On 18 August 2008 the Koshi River breached its eastern embankment near Kusaha in Sunsari and shifted into an old channel. Floodwater inundated settlements and agricultural land in eastern Nepal and affected communities across the border in India. The event showed how river dynamics, embankment condition, sedimentation and exposure can combine into a transboundary disaster.','More than 200 across wider affected region; totals vary','Large numbers injured/displaced','Major river and embankment failure','Large areas of farmland and settlements were inundated and many households required prolonged assistance.','Government of Nepal; World Bank; ICIMOD; UN disaster assessments',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2012 Seti River Flash Flood','2012-seti-river-flash-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2012-05-05','2012','Seti River, Kaski and Pokhara area','A sudden destructive flood/debris-flow event on the Seti River caused major loss of life near Pokhara.','On 5 May 2012 a sudden surge of water and debris travelled down the Seti River near Pokhara. The event caused widespread destruction along the river corridor and killed many people. The sudden nature of the disaster highlighted the danger of high-mountain source processes and limited warning time in narrow valleys.','Dozens reported; exact totals vary','Reported injuries/missing','Sudden flash flood/debris flow','Settlements, bridges and riverbank infrastructure were damaged.','Government of Nepal disaster reports; ICIMOD and scientific studies',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2014 Jure Landslide','2014-jure-landslide',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='landslide'),'2014-08-02','2014','Jure, Sindhupalchok','A massive landslide buried settlements, blocked the Sunkoshi River and formed a temporary lake.','On 2 August 2014 a massive slope failure occurred at Jure. ICIMOD reports about 6 million cubic metres of material entered the valley, forming a temporary lake of about 8 million cubic metres. The event killed 156 people and disrupted the Arniko Highway. Emergency teams worked to reduce the downstream outburst-flood threat.','156','Reported injuries; many displaced','Large rock/debris landslide','Settlements were buried, the Arniko Highway was disrupted and downstream communities faced flood risk.','ICIMOD; Government of Nepal; Department of Water Induced Disaster Management',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2015 Earthquake-Triggered Landslides','2015-earthquake-triggered-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='landslide'),'2015-04-25','2015','Central and northern Nepal','The 2015 earthquake triggered thousands of landslides across the Himalayan and mid-hill regions.','The Mw 7.8 Gorkha earthquake destabilized slopes over a huge area. Landslides blocked roads, buried settlements, damaged trekking routes and isolated mountain communities. Major slope failures and rock avalanches occurred around Langtang. Monsoon rainfall later reactivated unstable slopes.','Included within overall earthquake toll; separate total varies','Included within overall earthquake totals','Earthquake-triggered slope failures','Roads, trails, villages and rivers were affected and some slopes remained unstable for years.','USGS; ICIMOD; Government of Nepal; peer-reviewed research',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2017 Terai Monsoon Floods','2017-terai-monsoon-floods',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2017-08-11','2017','Terai and southern Nepal','Exceptional monsoon rainfall in August 2017 caused widespread flooding across southern Nepal.','The 2017 monsoon brought intense rainfall to the Terai and other parts of Nepal. The World Bank estimated about 1.7 million people were affected and damages and losses were around US$585 million. Homes, farmland, roads, bridges, schools and health facilities were affected.','More than 140 reported in Nepal','Hundreds reported','Exceptional monsoon rainfall','Large areas of farmland and settlements were inundated and transport, health and education services were disrupted.','Government of Nepal Post Disaster Needs Assessment; World Bank; UN OCHA; DHM',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2021 Melamchi Flood and Debris Flow','2021-melamchi-flood-debris-flow',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2021-06-15','2021','Melamchi and Helambu, Sindhupalchok','A catastrophic flood and debris-flow event struck the Melamchi and Helambu valleys.','On 15 June 2021 an extreme flood and debris-flow event struck Melamchi and Helambu. ICIMOD reported five deaths and 20 people missing in its immediate assessment. Homes, bridges, roads, hydropower facilities and the Melamchi Water Supply Project were damaged.','5 deaths; 20 missing in immediate ICIMOD assessment','Not consistently reported','Extreme flood/debris flow','Bridges, roads, homes, hydropower and water-supply infrastructure were damaged.','ICIMOD; Government of Nepal; NDRRMA',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2021 October Floods and Landslides','2021-october-floods-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2021-10-18','2021','Multiple districts','Unusually heavy post-monsoon rainfall caused widespread floods and landslides in October 2021.','In October 2021 unusually heavy rainfall after the normal monsoon caused floods and landslides across many parts of Nepal. The timing made the event particularly disruptive. Government reporting recorded substantial deaths, infrastructure losses and agricultural damage, with totals varying by reporting cut-off.','Dozens reported; final total depends on reporting period','Many reported injuries','Extreme post-monsoon rainfall','Roads, bridges, homes, crops and services were damaged.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; UN situation reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2024 Nepal Monsoon Floods and Landslides','2024-nepal-monsoon-floods-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2024-09-27','2024','Central and eastern Nepal including Kathmandu region','Extreme late-September rainfall caused severe floods and landslides across Nepal.','In late September 2024 exceptionally heavy rainfall caused severe flooding and landslides in multiple parts of Nepal. Kathmandu Valley and surrounding districts were among the hardest-hit areas. Roads, bridges, homes and public infrastructure suffered major damage. Final figures should follow the Government of Nepal’s consolidated assessment rather than early provisional media counts.','Official totals vary by assessment date','Hundreds reported in the wider disaster period','Extreme rainfall and river flooding','Homes, roads, bridges, agricultural land and public infrastructure were damaged.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; UN and World Bank assessments',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1981 Zhangzangbo Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','1981-zhangzangbo-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'1981-07-11','1981','Zhangzangbo Valley and Sun Koshi River','The 1981 Zhangzangbo GLOF released an enormous volume of water and caused major damage along the Sun Koshi corridor.','On 11 July 1981 the Zhangzangbo/Cirenmaco GLOF released an estimated 19 million cubic metres of water in about one hour. ICIMOD reports five deaths in Nepal and hundreds injured. The flood destroyed the Friendship Bridge, damaged the Sun Koshi hydropower system and severely affected sections of the Arniko Highway.','5 reported in Nepal','Hundreds reported','GLOF; about 19 million m3 released in about one hour','Bridge, hydropower and highway infrastructure were severely damaged and trade and transport were disrupted.','ICIMOD; historical GLOF inventories; Nepal government technical reports',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1985 Dig Tsho Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','1985-dig-tsho-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'1985-08-04','1985','Dig Tsho, Khumbu, Solukhumbu','The 1985 Dig Tsho GLOF destroyed a hydropower plant and infrastructure downstream.','On 4 August 1985 a GLOF from Dig Tsho sent a destructive surge down the Dudh Koshi system. ICIMOD records destruction of the nearly completed Namche hydropower plant, bridges, trails and cultivated land and loss of life.','Lives lost; exact total varies','Not consistently reported','GLOF','Namche hydropower, bridges, trails and agricultural land were damaged or destroyed.','ICIMOD GLOF inventories; Nepal government technical reports',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1991 Chubung Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','1991-chubung-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'1991-01-01','1991','Khumbu/Rolwaling region','A Chubung GLOF is included in historical inventories of GLOFs affecting Nepal.','The 1991 Chubung event is documented in Himalayan GLOF inventories. The public record is less detailed than for the 1981 and 1985 events, so this article deliberately avoids unsupported precise casualty and damage numbers.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','GLOF','Downstream channels and infrastructure were affected; detailed loss estimates are limited.','ICIMOD historical GLOF inventory',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1998 Tam Pokhari Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','1998-tam-pokhari-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'1998-09-03','1998','Tam Pokhari, Inkhu Khola, Solukhumbu','An ice avalanche entered Tam Pokhari and triggered a destructive GLOF.','On 3 September 1998 an ice avalanche entered Tam Pokhari and generated a wave that breached the moraine dam. ICIMOD reports approximately NPR 156 million in damage and that lives were lost.','Some lives lost; exact total varies','Not consistently reported','GLOF triggered by ice avalanche','Downstream infrastructure and settlements were damaged.','ICIMOD; historical GLOF research',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2017 Langmale Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','2017-langmale-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'2017-05-18','2017','Barun Valley, Makalu region','A GLOF affected the Barun Valley in eastern Nepal in 2017.','The Langmale GLOF occurred in the Barun Valley in 2017. It affected the high-mountain river system and demonstrated how changing glaciers and lakes can create sudden downstream hazards. Detailed event-level casualty and loss records are limited.','No confirmed major loss of life established in sources used','Not consistently reported','GLOF','High-mountain river channels and infrastructure were affected.','ICIMOD; Himalayan cryosphere and GLOF studies',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2024 Thame Glacial Lake Outburst Flood','2024-thame-glof',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='glof'),'2024-08-16','2024','Thame, Solukhumbu','A GLOF swept through Thame after the breach of glacial lakes upstream.','On 16 August 2024 a GLOF struck Thame. ICIMOD initially identified Thyanbo glacial lake as the source; a later NDRRMA-ICIMOD investigation described successive breaching of Upper and Lower Ngole Cho lakes about 10 km upstream. The flood destroyed or damaged homes, a school, a health post, hotels, bridges and other infrastructure and displaced residents.','No major confirmed loss of life in initial ICIMOD assessment','Not consistently reported','Glacial lake outburst flood','Initial ICIMOD assessment documented 14 destroyed properties; later assessment reported widespread damage and displacement of 135 people.','ICIMOD; NDRRMA; DHM; ICIMOD 2025 Thame Valley GLOF study',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2014 Annapurna Snowstorm and Avalanche Disaster','2014-annapurna-snowstorm',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='avalanche'),'2014-10-14','2014','Annapurna Circuit, Manang and Mustang','A severe October 2014 snowstorm and associated avalanches struck trekkers and mountain communities.','In October 2014 a severe snowstorm associated with Cyclone Hudhud produced heavy snow and blizzard conditions on the Annapurna Circuit. Trekkers and local people were caught in rapidly changing conditions, with avalanches and exposure contributing to deaths.','At least 43 reported','Many injured/rescued','Severe snowstorm and avalanche conditions','Trekkers died or required rescue; high passes and trails became dangerous.','Government of Nepal Ministry of Culture, Tourism and Civil Aviation; Himalayan rescue records; scientific studies',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2019 Bara-Parsa Tornado','2019-bara-parsa-tornado',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='tornado'),'2019-03-31','2019','Bara and Parsa','A rare violent tornado struck southern Nepal on 31 March 2019.','A severe convective storm produced a destructive tornado in Bara and Parsa. Homes were damaged or destroyed and the event caused deaths and hundreds of injuries. The disaster demonstrated the need for severe-weather observation, public warnings and safer construction in the Terai.','29','Hundreds','Tornado/severe rotating convective storm','Homes, roofs, electricity and local infrastructure were heavily damaged.','Government of Nepal disaster assessment; DHM; NDRRMA; meteorological studies',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('2016 Nepal Wildfire Season','2016-nepal-wildfire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'2016-04-01','2016','Multiple districts across Nepal','The 2016 dry-season wildfire period was a notable wildfire season affecting forests, air quality and communities.','Nepal experiences recurring dry-season forest fires before the summer monsoon. The 2016 season affected forests in numerous districts. Fire danger is influenced by dry vegetation, rainfall deficits, wind and human ignition. Satellite fire monitoring has become an important part of national wildfire observation.','Varies by incident','Varies by incident','Widespread dry-season wildfire activity','Forest ecosystems, air quality, biodiversity, agricultural land and nearby settlements were affected.','Department of Forests and Soil Conservation; ICIMOD; NASA FIRMS',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2021 Nepal Wildfire Season','2021-nepal-wildfire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'2021-03-01','2021','Multiple districts across Nepal','Nepal experienced widespread wildfire activity in the dry season of 2021, with extensive smoke and air-quality impacts.','The dry season of 2021 produced widespread wildfire activity across Nepal. Satellite monitoring showed extensive fire activity and smoke affected populated areas during periods of poor atmospheric dispersion. The season illustrates how dry conditions, vegetation, wind and human ignition can combine into national-scale wildfire and air-quality problems.','Multiple deaths reported across incidents; no single wildfire toll','Multiple injuries reported across incidents','Widespread wildfire activity','Forests and biodiversity were damaged and smoke affected air quality over broad areas.','ICIMOD; NASA FIRMS; Government of Nepal forest and disaster reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('Major Nepal Lightning Hazard','major-nepal-lightning-hazard',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='lightning'),'2019-04-01','Recent decades','Terai, hills and mountain districts','Lightning is a recurring high-fatality hazard in Nepal, especially during pre-monsoon and monsoon seasons.','Lightning strikes frequently occur during Nepal’s convective storm seasons. People working in agriculture, walking outdoors or sheltering under isolated trees are particularly vulnerable. Government disaster statistics show repeated deaths and injuries across Nepal. This article is a hazard-history entry; individual incidents should be added as separate records when available.','Annual totals vary; use government incident records','Annual totals vary','Severe convective thunderstorms','Deaths, injuries, livestock losses, fires and electrical damage occur every year.','Department of Hydrology and Meteorology; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal; Ministry of Home Affairs statistics',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('Major Nepal Hailstorm and Windstorm Hazard','major-nepal-hailstorm-windstorm-hazard',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='storm'),'2019-01-01','Recent decades','Terai, hills and mountain districts','Hailstorms, damaging winds and severe thunderstorms are recurring hazards across Nepal.','Severe thunderstorms can produce hail, strong winds, lightning and intense short-duration rainfall. These events damage crops, roofs, greenhouses, electricity infrastructure and communications. Agriculture is especially vulnerable because a localized hailstorm can destroy seasonal crops rapidly.','Varies by event','Varies by event','Severe thunderstorm, hail and wind','Agriculture, roofs, power lines and local infrastructure can be damaged.','Department of Hydrology and Meteorology; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('Nepal Drought and Dry-Season Risk','nepal-drought-history-and-risk',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='drought'),'2009-01-01','2008-2009','Western, mid-western and far-western Nepal','Drought often develops gradually through deficient winter or monsoon rainfall and produces agricultural and water-security impacts.','Drought develops over weeks or months rather than as a single sudden event. Nepal has experienced recurring agricultural drought, particularly when winter or monsoon rainfall is deficient. Western and mid-western farming communities can be especially vulnerable. Impacts include reduced crop yields, livestock stress, drinking-water shortages and food-security pressure.','No single disaster death toll','Livelihood and food-security impacts','Seasonal rainfall deficit','Agriculture, livestock, drinking water and rural livelihoods can be affected.','DHM; Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock Development; FAO; Government of Nepal assessments',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('Nepal Terai Heat Wave Hazard','nepal-terai-heat-wave-hazard',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='heat-wave'),'2024-05-01','Recent decades','Terai and southern plains','Extreme heat is an important and increasingly concerning hazard in Nepal’s Terai.','The Terai regularly experiences very high temperatures during late spring and early summer. Heat risk is increased by humidity, urbanization, limited shade, outdoor work and inadequate access to cooling and drinking water. Heat waves are not always recorded as discrete disasters with reliable national mortality figures, so individual episodes should be linked to official weather and health records.','Event-specific mortality varies','Heat-related illness varies','Extreme high temperature','Health, labor productivity, agriculture, livestock and water demand can be affected.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; WHO heat-health guidance',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('Nepal Terai Cold Wave Hazard','nepal-terai-cold-wave-hazard',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='cold-wave'),'2019-01-01','Recent decades','Terai and southern plains','Cold waves, dense fog and prolonged winter chill periodically affect Nepal’s Terai.','Winter cold waves are recurring hazards in southern Nepal. Dense fog and low temperatures affect transport, schools, agriculture and vulnerable people. Impacts are often greatest among people without adequate heating and among older adults and children.','Event-specific mortality varies','Cold-related illness varies','Low temperature and persistent fog','Health, transport, agriculture and livestock can be affected.','DHM; Government of Nepal winter disaster reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2020 Nepal Monsoon Floods and Landslides','2020-nepal-monsoon-floods-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2020-07-01','2020','Multiple districts','The 2020 monsoon produced widespread floods and landslides across Nepal.','During the 2020 monsoon heavy rainfall triggered floods and landslides across numerous districts. Mountain roads were repeatedly blocked, houses were damaged and agricultural land was affected. The disaster occurred during the COVID-19 pandemic, complicating evacuation and relief.','Season total varies by reporting cut-off','Many reported','Monsoon flood and rainfall-triggered landslides','Roads, bridges, homes, farms and local infrastructure were damaged.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; UN situation reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2022 Nepal Monsoon Floods and Landslides','2022-nepal-monsoon-floods-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2022-06-01','2022','Multiple districts','The 2022 monsoon produced repeated floods and landslides across Nepal.','Monsoon rainfall in 2022 triggered repeated floods, landslides and road disruptions. Impacts included deaths, damaged homes, blocked highways, crop losses and disruption to local services. The season consisted of many separate incidents rather than one single disaster.','Season total varies by official reporting period','Many reported','Monsoon rainfall','Transport, agriculture, housing and local infrastructure were repeatedly affected.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2023 Nepal Monsoon Floods and Landslides','2023-nepal-monsoon-floods-landslides',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2023-06-01','2023','Multiple districts','Floods and landslides during the 2023 monsoon caused repeated casualties and infrastructure damage.','The 2023 monsoon produced numerous localized floods, landslides and debris flows. Mountain highways and rural roads were particularly vulnerable to slope failure, while river flooding affected settlements and agricultural land. Individual incident records are more useful than one national event total.','Season total varies by official reporting period','Many reported','Monsoon rainfall','Roads, bridges, homes, farms and river corridors were affected.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2025 Nepal Monsoon Flood and Landslide Events','2025-nepal-monsoon-flood-landslide-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2025-06-01','2025','Multiple districts','Nepal continued to experience recurring monsoon floods, landslides and debris flows in 2025.','The 2025 monsoon produced multiple localized flood and landslide disasters affecting highways, bridges, settlements, agriculture and hydropower infrastructure. Because the season consisted of many incidents, final casualty and damage totals should be taken from the consolidated Government of Nepal database.','Season total varies by official reporting period','Many reported','Monsoon rainfall','Transport, settlements, agriculture and infrastructure were repeatedly disrupted.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2026 Rasuwa High-Mountain Flash Flood Disaster','2026-rasuwa-high-mountain-flash-flood',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='flood'),'2026-08-26','2026','Rasuwa and northern Nepal','A major high-mountain flash flood struck Rasuwa in August 2026, highlighting cryosphere-linked flood and debris-flow risk.','On 26 August 2026 a major flash flood swept through Rasuwa district in northern Nepal. The event affected settlements and infrastructure along the mountain river corridor and raised concerns about downstream flooding. Because the disaster is recent, casualty and damage assessments can change as search-and-rescue operations and official investigations continue.','Ongoing assessment; final total not established','Ongoing assessment','High-mountain flash flood/debris-flow event','Roads, bridges, settlements and border-area infrastructure were affected; downstream risk required monitoring.','ICIMOD 26 August 2026 media advisory; Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM',1,'PUBLISHED'),

('1987 Eastern Nepal Earthquake','1987-eastern-nepal-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1987-01-01','1987','Eastern Nepal','A damaging earthquake affected eastern Nepal and is included in national historical earthquake records.','The 1987 event affected communities in eastern Nepal, where rural masonry and unreinforced buildings were vulnerable to shaking. Historical summaries provide limited event-level detail, so this record is intentionally cautious about casualties and magnitude.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Historical earthquake; magnitude varies by catalogue','Local buildings and infrastructure were damaged in affected districts.','NSET historical earthquake catalogue; Government of Nepal records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('1994 Nepal Earthquake Sequence','1994-nepal-earthquake-sequence',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1994-01-01','1994','Central and western Nepal','A sequence of earthquakes in 1994 caused localized damage and renewed concern about Himalayan seismic risk.','Several moderate earthquakes were recorded in Nepal during 1994. The available public summaries do not support one definitive national casualty or damage total. Earthquake sequences can produce repeated shaking and increase the vulnerability of already damaged buildings.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate earthquake sequence','Localized structural damage and disruption were reported in affected communities.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS earthquake records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('1997 Bajura Earthquake','1997-bajura-earthquake',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'1997-01-01','1997','Bajura and far-western Nepal','A historical earthquake affected remote communities in far-western Nepal.','The 1997 Bajura event is recorded in historical earthquake listings for Nepal. Remoteness, difficult terrain and limited reporting capacity made contemporaneous damage assessment difficult. This entry should be expanded with district-level government records where available.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Magnitude not consistently reported','Rural homes, roads and local services may have been affected.','NSET earthquake catalogue; district administration records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2001 Nepal Himalayan Earthquake Activity','2001-nepal-himalayan-earthquake-activity',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2001-01-01','2001','Nepal Himalaya','Earthquake activity in 2001 included moderate events felt across parts of Nepal.','Nepal lies along an active collision zone and experiences frequent earthquakes below the threshold of major disaster. The 2001 record illustrates the importance of maintaining monitoring and preparedness even when an individual event causes limited damage.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate regional seismicity','Limited local effects were reported in available summaries.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS earthquake records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2005 Nepal Earthquake Events','2005-nepal-earthquake-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2005-01-01','2005','Nepal and Himalayan region','Moderate earthquakes in 2005 were felt in parts of Nepal and contributed to the long record of Himalayan seismic activity.','The 2005 events are best understood as a group of moderate earthquakes rather than one single national disaster. Public records do not provide a consistent consolidated loss total, but the events reinforce the need for resilient construction and local preparedness.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate Himalayan earthquakes','Localized shaking and minor damage were possible in affected areas.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2007 Nepal Earthquake Events','2007-nepal-earthquake-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2007-01-01','2007','Nepal Himalaya','Nepal recorded several moderate seismic events in 2007, with effects varying by location and building vulnerability.','The 2007 earthquake record includes felt events across the Himalayan region. Because many records combine felt reports with instrument observations, casualty and damage figures should be taken from individual event reports rather than inferred from the year alone.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate seismic events','Localized shaking and minor structural effects were reported in some areas.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS earthquake records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2010 Nepal Earthquake Events','2010-nepal-earthquake-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2010-01-01','2010','Nepal and adjoining Himalayan region','Moderate seismic events in 2010 affected parts of Nepal without a single consolidated national disaster toll.','The 2010 record shows how frequent smaller earthquakes form part of the background hazard in Nepal. Stronger local effects depend on depth, distance, soil conditions and construction quality.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate Himalayan seismicity','Localized shaking was reported; no single nationwide damage estimate is used here.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS earthquake records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2014 Nepal Earthquake Events','2014-nepal-earthquake-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='earthquake'),'2014-01-01','2014','Nepal Himalaya','Moderate earthquakes recorded before the 2015 disaster affected communities and provided another reminder of regional seismic exposure.','Nepal experienced multiple felt earthquakes in 2014. The available summaries do not support treating them as one event or assigning a combined casualty figure. They are included as a historical activity record for researchers reviewing the lead-up to 2015.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Moderate regional earthquakes','Localized shaking and minor damage were reported in some locations.','NSET earthquake catalogue; USGS',0,'PUBLISHED'),

