('2015 Nepal Drought and Water Stress','2015-nepal-drought-and-water-stress',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='drought'),'2015-01-01','2015','Western and mid-western Nepal','Dry conditions and water stress affected some communities during the 2015 agricultural year.','Drought impacts can coexist with other disasters and are often overshadowed by sudden events. In 2015, local water availability, crop conditions and post-earthquake vulnerability varied widely by district, so this record does not assign a single national drought toll.','No single disaster death toll','Livelihood and water-security impacts','Seasonal rainfall deficit and water stress','Agriculture, livestock and household water access were affected in some districts.','DHM; FAO; Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock Development',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2010 Terai Heat Wave','2010-terai-heat-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='heat-wave'),'2010-05-01','2010','Terai plains','High temperatures in the Terai created seasonal heat stress for outdoor workers and vulnerable people.','The Terai can experience dangerous heat before the monsoon. Risk increases where shade, drinking water and healthcare are limited. Historical health reporting does not consistently separate heat-related illness from other causes, so no unsupported mortality figure is used here.','Event-specific mortality varies','Heat-related illness varies','Extreme pre-monsoon heat','Health, labor, livestock, crops and water demand were affected.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; WHO heat-health guidance',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2016 Nepal Heat Wave','2016-nepal-heat-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='heat-wave'),'2016-05-01','2016','Terai and southern plains','A period of extreme pre-monsoon heat affected the Terai in 2016.','Heat waves can be intensified by humidity, dense settlements, limited shade and outdoor work. This event record should be paired with station observations and health surveillance because temperatures and impacts differed between districts.','Event-specific mortality varies','Heat-related illness varies','Extreme high temperature','People, livestock, crops and water systems were exposed to heat stress.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; WHO heat-health guidance',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2022 Nepal Heat Wave','2022-nepal-heat-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='heat-wave'),'2022-05-01','2022','Terai plains','High temperatures and delayed monsoon conditions created heat stress across parts of the Terai in 2022.','The 2022 heat period shows why heat preparedness needs clear thresholds, public messaging and protection for outdoor workers. Official impact estimates should be preferred over social-media or media-only counts.','Event-specific mortality varies','Heat-related illness varies','Extreme high temperature','Health, labor productivity, agriculture, livestock and water demand were affected.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; WHO heat-health guidance',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('2003 Nepal Cold Wave','2003-nepal-cold-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='cold-wave'),'2003-01-01','2003','Terai plains','Persistent winter fog and low temperatures affected vulnerable communities in the Terai during 2003.','Cold waves are often undercounted because they develop over several days and their health impacts may be recorded under broader winter illness categories. This record groups the hazard period without claiming a precise national death toll.','Event-specific mortality varies','Cold-related illness varies','Low temperature and persistent fog','Health, transport, crops, livestock and schools were affected.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; Government of Nepal winter reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2011 Nepal Cold Wave','2011-nepal-cold-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='cold-wave'),'2011-01-01','2011','Terai and southern plains','A winter cold wave affected the Terai through low temperatures, fog and disruption to daily life.','Cold-wave impacts can be severe for people without insulated housing or heating. Dense fog also reduces road and aviation visibility. District-level records are needed to separate this season from normal winter conditions.','Event-specific mortality varies','Cold-related illness varies','Low temperature and persistent fog','Health, transport, agriculture and livestock were affected.','DHM; Government of Nepal winter disaster reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2023 Nepal Cold Wave','2023-nepal-cold-wave',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='cold-wave'),'2023-01-01','2023','Terai and southern plains','Cold conditions and dense fog affected transport, schools, agriculture and vulnerable people in the Terai during 2023.','The 2023 winter record highlights the need for local cold-wave warnings and protection for older adults, children, outdoor workers and people in poorly heated homes. Exact health impacts vary by district and reporting method.','Event-specific mortality varies','Cold-related illness varies','Low temperature and persistent fog','Health, transport, crops, livestock and public services were affected.','DHM; Ministry of Health and Population; Government of Nepal winter reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1991 Nepal Forest Fire Season','1991-nepal-forest-fire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'1991-03-01','1991','Hills and Terai forests','Dry-season fires affected forests and rural land in Nepal during the early 1990s.','Forest-fire reporting was less systematic before satellite monitoring. Fires were often detected through local observation, and impacts on air quality and biodiversity were rarely measured consistently. This record should be expanded with forest district archives.','Varies by incident','Varies by incident','Dry-season wildfire activity','Forest ecosystems, wildlife, pasture and nearby farms were affected.','Department of Forests and Soil Conservation; historical district records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2000 Nepal Forest Fire Season','2000-nepal-forest-fire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'2000-03-01','2000','Hills and Terai forests','Dry vegetation and pre-monsoon conditions contributed to recurring forest fires across Nepal in 2000.','Wildfire risk increases when winter and spring rainfall is low, vegetation dries and wind spreads flames. Earlier seasons are difficult to compare because detection and reporting systems were less complete than today.','Varies by incident','Varies by incident','Dry-season wildfire activity','Forests, biodiversity, air quality and nearby settlements were exposed.','Department of Forests and Soil Conservation; FAO; historical district records',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2010 Nepal Forest Fire Season','2010-nepal-forest-fire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'2010-03-01','2010','Multiple districts across Nepal','Forest fires during the 2010 dry season affected forests, smoke levels and rural communities.','The 2010 season is included as a national wildfire record because fires occurred across multiple districts. Exact burned-area estimates depend on the detection method and should be checked against satellite products and forest inventories.','Varies by incident','Varies by incident','Widespread dry-season fires','Forests, air quality, wildlife habitat and local livelihoods were affected.','Department of Forests and Soil Conservation; ICIMOD; NASA FIRMS',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2024 Nepal Wildfire Season','2024-nepal-wildfire-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='wildfire'),'2024-03-01','2024','Multiple districts across Nepal','The 2024 dry season brought recurring wildfires, smoke and air-quality concerns across Nepal.','Wildfire activity before the monsoon can affect forests and communities over a wide area. Satellite fire detections show activity but do not by themselves establish burned area, cause or human loss; those details require ground verification.','Varies by incident','Varies by incident','Widespread dry-season wildfire activity','Forest ecosystems, air quality, biodiversity and nearby settlements were affected.','ICIMOD; NASA FIRMS; Department of Forests and Soil Conservation; DHM',0,'PUBLISHED'),

('1982 Nepal Debris-Flow Events','1982-nepal-debris-flow-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'1982-07-01','1982','Hill valleys and mountain roads','Debris flows repeatedly affected steep valleys during intense monsoon rainfall in the early 1980s.','Debris flows combine water, soil, rock and vegetation and can move faster than ordinary landslides. Historical national summaries often grouped them with floods or landslides, so this archive entry preserves the cross-category hazard without assigning unsupported totals.','Not reliably established','Not reliably established','Rainfall-triggered debris flow','River corridors, roads, bridges, homes and farmland were exposed.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; Department of Water Induced Disaster Management',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('1999 Nepal Wind and Rain Disasters','1999-nepal-wind-and-rain-disasters',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'1999-07-01','1999','Multiple districts','Combined wind, intense rain and localized flooding affected communities across Nepal in 1999.','Some disaster reports record compound weather events under broad categories such as storm, flood or other disaster. This entry is retained for search and historical discovery while district-level source records are reviewed.','Incident totals vary','Incident totals vary','Compound severe-weather event','Roofs, crops, drainage systems, homes and local roads were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; DHM; district administration reports',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2005 Nepal Multi-Hazard Monsoon Events','2005-nepal-multi-hazard-monsoon-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2005-07-01','2005','Multiple districts','The 2005 monsoon produced a combination of floods, landslides, debris flows and severe storms.','Monsoon disaster seasons are not single hazards. Rainfall can trigger flooding in the plains, slope failure in the hills and debris flows in narrow valleys at the same time. This grouped record should be read with the individual hazard entries.','Season total varies by source','Many reported or displaced','Compound monsoon hazard','Homes, farmland, roads, bridges and local services were affected.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; DHM; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2013 Nepal Multi-Hazard Monsoon Events','2013-nepal-multi-hazard-monsoon-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2013-07-01','2013','Multiple districts','The 2013 monsoon produced interacting floods, landslides, lightning and severe storms across Nepal.','A national archive benefits from recording compound seasons because the same rainfall system can create different impacts in different terrain. Precise totals should be taken from annual government reporting and not inferred from this grouped story.','Season total varies by source','Many reported or displaced','Compound monsoon hazard','River flooding, slope failures, road blockages, crop losses and service disruption occurred.','Government of Nepal disaster-risk profile; DHM; NDRRMA',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2018 Nepal Multi-Hazard Monsoon Events','2018-nepal-multi-hazard-monsoon-events',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2018-07-01','2018','Multiple districts','Floods, landslides, lightning and severe storms occurred across Nepal during the 2018 monsoon.','The 2018 season illustrates why disaster records should link weather, terrain and exposure. Different districts experienced different combinations of hazards, and national totals changed as new incidents were reported.','Season total varies by official reporting period','Many reported or displaced','Compound monsoon hazard','Transport, settlements, agriculture, hydropower and local services were affected.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; Nepal Disaster Risk Reduction Portal',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2021 Nepal Compound Disaster Season','2021-nepal-compound-disaster-season',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2021-06-01','2021','Multiple districts','Nepal experienced earthquakes, floods, debris flows, landslides, fires and severe weather during 2021.','The 2021 archive record includes several hazard types rather than one event. Compound and consecutive disasters can stretch emergency capacity, damage the same infrastructure repeatedly and make recovery more difficult. Individual stories should remain the authoritative source for each incident.','Season total varies by hazard and source','Many reported or displaced','Multiple hazards','Housing, roads, bridges, water systems, farms and public services were affected.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; ICIMOD; sector assessments',0,'PUBLISHED'),
('2024 Nepal Compound Monsoon Disaster','2024-nepal-compound-monsoon-disaster',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2024-09-27','2024','Central and eastern Nepal','Late September 2024 combined extreme rainfall, river flooding, landslides and transport disruption.','The 2024 disaster period shows how one extreme rainfall episode can affect urban valleys, hill roads and lowland rivers at the same time. Early reports were provisional; final figures should follow the consolidated Government of Nepal assessment and distinguish deaths, missing people and displaced households.','Official totals vary by assessment date','Hundreds reported in the wider disaster period','Compound extreme-rainfall event','Homes, roads, bridges, farms, schools and public infrastructure were damaged.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; UN and World Bank assessments',1,'PUBLISHED'),
('2024 Nepal Compound Monsoon Disaster','2024-nepal-compound-monsoon-disaster',(SELECT id FROM categories WHERE slug='other'),'2024-09-27','2024','Central and eastern Nepal','Late September 2024 combined extreme rainfall, river flooding, landslides and transport disruption.','The 2024 disaster period shows how one extreme rainfall episode can affect urban valleys, hill roads and lowland rivers at the same time. Early reports were provisional; final figures should follow the consolidated Government of Nepal assessment and distinguish deaths, missing people and displaced households.','Official totals vary by assessment date','Hundreds reported in the wider disaster period','Compound extreme-rainfall event','Homes, roads, bridges, farms, schools and public infrastructure were damaged.','Government of Nepal/NDRRMA; DHM; UN and World Bank assessments',1,'PUBLISHED');

-- Add a longer encyclopedia-style context paragraph to every published story.
UPDATE stories s
JOIN categories c ON c.id = s.category_id
SET s.content = CONCAT(s.content, '\n\n',
CASE c.slug
 WHEN 'earthquake' THEN 'Earthquakes in Nepal are associated with the ongoing collision between the Indian and Eurasian tectonic plates, which drives shortening and uplift across the Himalaya. The hazard is shaped not only by the size of an earthquake but also by depth, distance from populated places, local ground conditions, building materials and the ability of roads, hospitals and communications systems to remain operational. Historical accounts frequently use approximate dates, reconstructed magnitudes and changing administrative boundaries, while modern assessments may revise casualty and damage totals as field surveys continue. For that reason, this article should be read alongside the cited catalogue or government assessment, with estimates retained as estimates and later revisions documented rather than silently replaced.'
 WHEN 'flood' THEN 'Flood disasters in Nepal reflect the interaction of monsoon rainfall, snowmelt, steep tributaries, sediment movement, river morphology and settlement on flood-prone land. The same weather system may produce rapid flash flooding in a mountain valley, prolonged inundation in the Terai and landslides on connecting roads. Damage is often greater where bridges, embankments, homes and public services have been built in exposed corridors or where early warning cannot reach communities in time. Event totals should identify the reporting date and distinguish deaths, missing people, displaced households, affected people and economic damage.'
 WHEN 'landslide' THEN 'Landslides are common across the middle hills and mountain valleys because steep terrain, fractured rock, intense rainfall and active river erosion combine with roads, settlement expansion and changing land use. A slide may begin as a shallow failure beside a road or become a large debris flow that blocks a river and threatens communities downstream. Earthquake shaking can leave slopes unstable for years, while later monsoon rain can reactivate cracks and scarps. Reliable interpretation therefore requires attention to the date of movement, the triggering process, the size of the slide, the exposed population and the quality of the source survey.'
 WHEN 'avalanche' THEN 'Avalanche risk in Nepal is concentrated in high mountain terrain where snowfall, wind loading, rapid temperature change, serac collapse and unstable slopes can release snow and ice onto climbing routes, trails and settlements. Historical reporting is often strongest for expeditions and popular trekking corridors, while losses in remote valleys may be incompletely recorded. The apparent severity of an avalanche depends on its path, timing, depth, terrain and the number of people present, so a report should separate deaths, injuries, missing people, rescues and route closures. Expedition records, local administration reports and technical snow studies provide complementary evidence.'
 WHEN 'glof' THEN 'Glacial lake outburst floods, commonly abbreviated as GLOFs, occur when a moraine, ice dam or other natural barrier fails and releases stored lake water, sediment and ice into a downstream valley. In Nepal, lake growth is linked to glacier retreat, ice collapse, changing precipitation and the geometry of high mountain basins, although each lake has its own history and failure mechanisms. A GLOF can travel rapidly through narrow channels and damage bridges, hydropower, trails, farmland and settlements far below the lake. Inventory dates and lake names sometimes differ between publications, so event descriptions should distinguish confirmed outbursts from hazard assessments and possible future scenarios.'
 WHEN 'lightning' THEN 'Lightning is a recurring atmospheric hazard in Nepal, particularly during pre-monsoon and monsoon thunderstorms. Exposure is increased when people are working in fields, travelling on foot, gathering beneath isolated trees or using poorly protected buildings and electrical equipment. Unlike a single large disaster, the national burden is usually made up of many local incidents whose details arrive through district reporting systems at different times. A responsible historical account should therefore state whether a number is an annual total, a preliminary count or an incident-specific figure, and should give equal attention to prevention measures such as safe shelter, public warnings and school procedures.'
 WHEN 'storm' THEN 'Severe storms in Nepal may combine hail, damaging wind, lightning, intense short-duration rain and, in some places, flash flooding. Their impacts can be highly localized: a single storm cell may destroy crops and roofs in one municipality while nearby stations record much less severe weather. Agricultural losses are particularly difficult to compare because crop stage, protected cultivation, livestock exposure and access to insurance vary between communities. Weather-station observations, radar or satellite evidence, local damage surveys and government relief records should be considered together when reconstructing an event.'
 WHEN 'tornado' THEN 'Tornadoes and tornado-like rotating windstorms are uncommon in Nepal but can produce concentrated destruction over a narrow path. Classification is difficult when an event has not been observed by radar or surveyed soon after the damage, because straight-line winds, downbursts and rotating storms can leave similar local evidence. A wiki-style record should identify the reporting authority, describe the affected path and avoid treating every severe wind report as a confirmed tornado. Homes, roofs, trees, crops, electricity lines and community buildings are important indicators of impact, while casualty figures should be linked to a dated official assessment.'
 WHEN 'drought' THEN 'Drought is a slow-onset hazard caused by a sustained mismatch between available water and the needs of people, ecosystems, crops or livestock. In Nepal it may follow deficient winter rain, a delayed or weak monsoon, prolonged dry spells, reduced spring water or a combination of these conditions. The effects are often uneven: one district may experience crop failure while another has adequate irrigation or rainfall. Historical analysis should distinguish meteorological drought from agricultural, hydrological and socioeconomic drought, and should describe food security, migration, livestock, drinking-water access and household coping strategies rather than relying only on a death toll.'
 WHEN 'heat-wave' THEN 'Heat waves in Nepal are most strongly associated with the Terai and southern plains, where high temperatures can combine with humidity, limited shade, outdoor labour, dense settlements and restricted access to cooling or medical care. Heat is often undercounted because illness may be recorded as dehydration, cardiovascular stress or another condition rather than as a disaster fatality. A useful historical record should include observed temperatures, duration, affected districts, vulnerable groups and public-health measures when those data are available. Heat warnings, drinking water, shaded rest, adjusted work hours and access to treatment are central parts of risk reduction.'
 WHEN 'cold-wave' THEN 'Cold waves in the Terai are commonly accompanied by persistent fog, low daytime temperatures and reduced visibility. The hazard affects people living in poorly insulated homes, older adults, children, outdoor workers, people with chronic illness, livestock and winter crops. Transport and school attendance may also be disrupted even when no single dramatic incident is recorded. Because cold-related deaths and illness can be attributed to several medical causes, historical totals are frequently uncertain. Records should therefore explain the duration and geographic extent of the cold period and identify the source used for any health estimate.'
 WHEN 'wildfire' THEN 'Wildfires in Nepal are most frequent during the dry period before the summer monsoon, when grasses, leaf litter and forest vegetation become flammable and wind can carry fire across slopes. Ignition may be accidental, agricultural or deliberate, and a satellite hotspot does not by itself prove the size, cause or severity of a ground fire. Smoke can affect distant towns and people with respiratory conditions even when flames remain far from settlements. A detailed archive entry should separate detected fire points, burned area, forest type, damage to homes or livelihoods, injuries, deaths and the effectiveness of suppression or community response.'
 ELSE 'Natural disasters in Nepal are shaped by the country\'s extreme geographic range, from the high Himalaya through steep middle hills to the densely settled Terai. A single season may involve several hazards at once, and the consequences depend on exposure, poverty, infrastructure quality, warning coverage, governance and access to emergency services. Historical records are strongest when they clearly separate observed facts, estimates, preliminary reports and later revisions. This article should therefore be updated with dated government assessments, technical studies and local evidence while preserving the uncertainty attached to older or incomplete records.'
END)
WHERE s.status = 'PUBLISHED'
	AND CASE c.slug
		WHEN 'earthquake' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Earthquakes in Nepal are associated with the ongoing collision%'
		WHEN 'flood' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Flood disasters in Nepal reflect the interaction%'
		WHEN 'landslide' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Landslides are common across the middle hills%'
		WHEN 'avalanche' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Avalanche risk in Nepal is concentrated%'
		WHEN 'glof' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Glacial lake outburst floods, commonly abbreviated%'
		WHEN 'lightning' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Lightning is a recurring atmospheric hazard%'
		WHEN 'storm' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Severe storms in Nepal may combine%'
		WHEN 'tornado' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Tornadoes and tornado-like rotating windstorms%'
		WHEN 'drought' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Drought is a slow-onset hazard%'
		WHEN 'heat-wave' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Heat waves in Nepal are most strongly associated%'
		WHEN 'cold-wave' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Cold waves in the Terai are commonly accompanied%'
		WHEN 'wildfire' THEN s.content NOT LIKE '%Wildfires in Nepal are most frequent%'
		ELSE s.content NOT LIKE '%Natural disasters in Nepal are shaped by the country%'
	END;

-- End of expanded archive dataset.
